Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Ava integrates with and can bundle third-party software and models that carry
their OWN licenses, which apply to those components. Notable examples:

  - Agent runtime: NVIDIA NemoClaw / OpenClaw (Apache-2.0,
    https://github.com/NVIDIA/NemoClaw), run in an OpenShell sandbox. Installed
    on demand (npm) and not redistributed in this repository.
  - Inference engines (e.g. vLLM, Ollama, llama.cpp) — their respective licenses.
  - Models / checkpoints you download (LLMs, the GPU model, upscalers, video models) —
    each has its own license and acceptable-use terms. Review before use.
  - the GPU service and its custom nodes — their respective licenses.
  - Python dependencies — see requirements*.txt; Node dependencies for the web
    app — see frontend/package.json — and their upstream licenses.

The installer/first-run flow surfaces model license terms where applicable. It
is the operator's responsibility to comply with the terms of any model or
component they choose to install.
